256
00:13:43,960 --> 00:13:45,397
Where are they going to take me?

257
00:13:45,480 --> 00:13:46,820
Say something, please.

258
00:13:47,100 --> 00:13:49,237
I have to know where they're taking me.

259
00:13:49,320 --> 00:13:50,457
What are they going to do?

260
00:13:50,540 --> 00:13:51,370
Rémy!

261
00:13:52,820 --> 00:13:53,650
Dunno.

262
00:13:53,733 --> 00:13:56,889
Although, I doubt you'll be
living in peace and tranquility.

263
00:14:17,360 --> 00:14:22,480
Now, at long last, we can
finally pass on, together.

264
00:14:32,900 --> 00:14:33,730
What?

265
00:14:33,813 --> 00:14:35,740
Are you really leaving us, Raimi?

266
00:14:36,620 --> 00:14:40,157
Surely it wouldn't hurt anything if
you stayed a little while longer.

267
00:14:40,240 --> 00:14:43,297
I mean, you've been like a
guardian angel to this town.

268
00:14:43,380 --> 00:14:45,397
I can't imagine life here without you.

269
00:14:45,480 --> 00:14:47,760
Please, you have to stay! Koichi,

270
00:14:48,060 --> 00:14:48,997
you're very sweet,

271
00:14:49,080 --> 00:14:52,557
but Arnold and I have done everything
we set out to accomplish here.

272
00:14:52,640 --> 00:14:54,875
The time's come for us to leave Morio.

273
00:14:55,120 --> 00:14:56,532
That's how it has to be.

274
00:14:57,440 --> 00:14:58,780
So, little Rohan,

275
00:14:58,940 --> 00:15:02,717
do you think you're going to cry after
we've gone off to the great beyond?

276
00:15:02,800 --> 00:15:04,020
In your dreams?

277
00:15:04,200 --> 00:15:06,137
What reason would I have to miss you?

278
00:15:06,220 --> 00:15:09,220
You died 15 years ago,
making you a distant memory.

279
00:15:09,680 --> 00:15:12,817
I've said this before, but
spirits should really just let go.

280
00:15:12,900 --> 00:15:15,697
Oh, haunting the world of the
living is so out of style.

281
00:15:15,780 --> 00:15:17,997
A soul's final resting
place isn't here with us,

282
00:15:18,080 --> 00:15:20,315
but exploring the uncharted afterlife.

283
00:15:28,020 --> 00:15:32,457
Fine, I'll say it alright, but I'm only
doing so because I'll never see you again!

284
00:15:32,540 --> 00:15:33,440
I'll miss you!

285
00:15:33,740 --> 00:15:35,780
Of course I don't want you to go!

286
00:15:39,620 --> 00:15:40,450
Yo!

287
00:15:42,900 --> 00:15:44,520
Hey, you're all here

288
00:15:45,580 --> 00:15:47,540
So it's all over Raimi.

289
00:15:47,960 --> 00:15:50,960
Oh wow looks like everyone showed up.

290
00:15:51,080 --> 00:15:52,786
We've all come to say goodbye

291
00:15:56,060 --> 00:15:57,140
You guys

292
00:15:57,780 --> 00:16:02,017
It feels weird to say this to the dearly
departed, but take care of yourself.

293
00:16:02,100 --> 00:16:03,865
See you on the other side, Kay

294
00:16:04,940 --> 00:16:07,580
You're an extraordinary young woman dear

295
00:16:14,940 --> 00:16:17,840
Oh, Raimi, thank you so
much for all you've done.

296
00:16:18,020 --> 00:16:20,957
You saved this little town when
it needed a savior the most.

297
00:16:21,040 --> 00:16:23,040
Thank you for saying that, Koichi.

298
00:16:23,180 --> 00:16:26,280
But we saved Morioh, all of us together.

299
00:16:26,640 --> 00:16:32,320
As long as we draw breath, no one here
today will ever forget you or your bravery.

300
00:16:32,880 --> 00:16:33,710
Thank you all.

301
00:16:33,793 --> 00:16:34,975
That means the world.

302
00:16:35,220 --> 00:16:36,357
So long, my friends.

303
00:16:36,440 --> 00:16:37,270
Be well.

304
00:16:39,340 --> 00:16:41,100
So long, Raimi. Godspeed.

305
00:16:52,480 --> 00:16:53,380
Rest easy.

306
00:16:57,220 --> 00:16:58,260
Where is he?

307
00:16:58,420 --> 00:16:59,500
It's so late.

308
00:17:00,200 --> 00:17:01,965
I guess he's working overtime.

309
00:17:02,260 --> 00:17:04,907
It would have been nice
if he called, though.

310
00:17:07,280 --> 00:17:08,380
Oh, Hayato!

311
00:17:08,660 --> 00:17:10,317
You haven't touched your food.

312
00:17:10,400 --> 00:17:11,717
Hurry up before it gets cold.

313
00:17:11,800 --> 00:17:14,976
If you're waiting for me,
I'll eat when Dad gets home.

314
00:17:18,720 --> 00:17:19,980
Uh, Hayato?

315
00:17:20,780 --> 00:17:21,820
It's okay, Mom.

316
00:17:22,080 --> 00:17:23,198
I'll wait with you.

317
00:17:23,920 --> 00:17:27,260
When Dad gets home, we'll all
sit down and eat together.

318
00:17:27,500 --> 00:17:29,794
Cause that's what a family does, right?

319
00:17:31,000 --> 00:17:31,830
Sure.

320
00:17:32,600 --> 00:17:34,597
Say, am I imagining things?

321
00:17:34,680 --> 00:17:36,621
Or have you gotten taller lately?

322
00:17:38,260 --> 00:17:42,700
When all was said and done, our little
Morio wasn't the town it used to be.

323
00:17:43,000 --> 00:17:45,917
A monster named Yoshikage
Kira swept in like

324
00:17:46,000 --> 00:17:48,765
a plague and had his way
with our beloved home.

325
00:17:49,740 --> 00:17:53,637
Hayato's mother will no doubt wait
for her husband until the end of time,

326
00:17:53,720 --> 00:17:56,097
and Shigechi's parents will never stop

327
00:17:56,180 --> 00:17:58,945
waiting for their special
little man to return.

328
00:17:59,560 --> 00:18:01,360
Whether a son, daughter,

329
00:18:01,700 --> 00:18:06,465
brother, or sister, Kira's victims belong
to parents who will never give up hope.

330
00:18:06,600 --> 00:18:10,320
And yet, that hope will only
cause their pain to grow deeper.

331
00:18:11,100 --> 00:18:14,460
The question is, what can
we do to lessen this burden?

332
00:18:15,720 --> 00:18:18,057
Will a vile past consume our future,

333
00:18:18,140 --> 00:18:21,258
or will we be able to forge
ahead unfettered by fear?

334
00:18:21,540 --> 00:18:22,980
I wish I could say.

335
00:18:24,500 --> 00:18:26,140
How about it, Jotaro?

336
00:18:26,940 --> 00:18:30,497
You worried about what might
happen when we leave this place?

337
00:18:30,580 --> 00:18:32,120
I am, just a bit.

338
00:18:32,660 --> 00:18:33,777
Because of all of this,

339
00:18:33,860 --> 00:18:37,557
we've had the chance to see how
capable Josuke and his friends are.

340
00:18:37,640 --> 00:18:40,934
And there's one thing I can
say with absolute certainty.

341
00:18:41,380 --> 00:18:45,000
The young people living in this
town are heroes one and all,

342
00:18:45,140 --> 00:18:47,817
and each one of them
possesses a heart of gold.

343
00:18:47,900 --> 00:18:51,317
They've the same righteous hearts we
witnessed on our journey to Egypt.

344
00:18:51,400 --> 00:18:56,106
They carry a spirit of radiance that will
fight for true justice above all else.

345
00:18:56,260 --> 00:18:59,180
I see it in Josuke, as well as the others.

346
00:19:00,520 --> 00:19:02,402
Morio's in good hands with them.

347
00:19:03,300 --> 00:19:06,577
As long as they're here, we
have nothing to worry about.

348
00:19:06,660 --> 00:19:07,820
Hey, old man!

349
00:19:08,180 --> 00:19:11,800
Don't just stand there
gawking! Answer me! Well then,

350
00:19:12,060 --> 00:19:13,917
guess it's time for me to say goodbye to a

351
00:19:14,000 --> 00:19:16,706
great son who's made his
father so very proud.

352
00:19:16,880 --> 00:19:20,077
Hey, remember that picture of
mom I gave you a while ago?

353
00:19:20,160 --> 00:19:21,857
You don't still have it, do you?

354
00:19:21,940 --> 00:19:22,822
Of course I do.

355
00:19:22,960 --> 00:19:26,197
I put it in my wallet for
safekeeping, just like you told me to.

356
00:19:26,280 --> 00:19:27,110
Ha!

357
00:19:27,193 --> 00:19:29,097
Since I can't tell her
in person, I'll tell you.

358
00:19:29,180 --> 00:19:31,651
I wish her all the happiness in the world.

359
00:19:32,540 --> 00:19:35,580
So, funny thing about
that picture I gave you.

360
00:19:35,800 --> 00:19:38,060
I decided to hang on to a piece.

361
00:19:40,040 --> 00:19:41,000
Shining Diamond!

362
00:19:44,440 --> 00:19:46,360
Oh wow, you shouldn't have!

363
00:19:46,600 --> 00:19:48,597
Though I'll take it if you insist.

364
00:19:48,680 --> 00:19:51,757
We'll just call this gift
16 years of back allowance.

365
00:19:51,840 --> 00:19:52,670
Besides,

366
00:19:52,753 --> 00:19:55,317
think about what your better half would
say if you took that picture over you!

367
00:19:55,400 --> 00:19:57,417
Who does that cocky punk think he is?

368
00:19:57,500 --> 00:20:00,324
I'm starting to see that
golden spirit, old man.

369
00:20:00,620 --> 00:20:03,149
And he's seeing it all
the way to the bank.

370
00:20:03,780 --> 00:20:05,640
You take good care of yourself!

371
00:20:11,600 --> 00:20:14,188
The invisible baby's
mother was never found.

372
00:20:14,300 --> 00:20:18,712
So Joseph Joestar rose to the occasion
and began an adventure as a new dad.

373
00:20:19,780 --> 00:20:22,637
Jotaro Kujo finally finished
a doctoral thesis he began

374
00:20:22,720 --> 00:20:25,657
on a species of starfish he
found on a beach in Morio,

375
00:20:25,740 --> 00:20:27,060
earning him his PhD.

376
00:20:28,500 --> 00:20:29,330
Ugh!

377
00:20:29,413 --> 00:20:30,600
Damn that Josuke!

378
00:20:30,960 --> 00:20:34,437
He's always coming in here and eating
all my food like he owns the place!

379
00:20:34,520 --> 00:20:35,350
Ugh!

380
00:20:35,460 --> 00:20:37,120
I'll just drink his juice.

381
00:20:38,260 --> 00:20:39,090
Koichi!

382
00:20:40,280 --> 00:20:41,420
Sorry I'm late.

383
00:20:41,780 --> 00:20:45,251
I was making Bind boxes for
us and lost track of the time.

384
00:20:45,460 --> 00:20:47,960
Wow, you actually made us a special lunch?

385
00:20:48,100 --> 00:20:49,335
That's so thoughtful!

386
00:20:49,440 --> 00:20:51,381
Lunchtime can't come soon enough!

387
00:21:01,740 --> 00:21:02,570
Tasty!

388
00:21:03,900 --> 00:21:04,730
Tasty!

389
00:21:08,000 --> 00:21:10,420
Now we're cooking, let the healing begin!

390
00:21:10,700 --> 00:21:12,994
Don't fight it, let the food carry you!

391
00:21:13,120 --> 00:21:17,020
If this works, you'll be a normal
old dad again, isn't that great?

392
00:21:21,360 --> 00:21:23,140
Well, that didn't work.

393
00:21:25,200 --> 00:21:27,020
My skin is so smooth!

394
00:21:27,180 --> 00:21:28,597
Check out my refreshed eyes!

395
00:21:28,680 --> 00:21:30,417
The food here is out of this world!

396
00:21:30,500 --> 00:21:31,497
Isn't it, though?

397
00:21:31,580 --> 00:21:34,677
Thanks to this food, I'm even
more stunningly gorgeous now.

398
00:21:34,760 --> 00:21:36,017
What am I gonna do with myself?

399
00:21:36,100 --> 00:21:37,337
You're simply radiant, you!

400
00:21:37,420 --> 00:21:38,917
Yeah, you're practically beaming!

401
00:21:39,000 --> 00:21:40,260
Mmm, you think so?

402
00:21:40,480 --> 00:21:44,440
Would you say I'm a dazzling dish
of devilish delights? Gotcha!

403
00:21:47,100 --> 00:21:49,560
Well, amigo mio, until next we meet.

404
00:21:50,420 --> 00:21:54,577
I just saw Ko holding hands with a
girl, and she was drop-dead gorgeous.

405
00:21:54,660 --> 00:21:58,737
Oh my, are you sure he never mentioned
anything to me about a girlfriend?

406
00:21:58,820 --> 00:22:02,220
Did you hear? Mr. Kira
went missing. Yeah, I did.

407
00:22:02,580 --> 00:22:06,340
They're saying they found him
dead, without a face. How freaky.

408
00:22:06,920 --> 00:22:08,577
And just how are you going
to make this up to me?

409
00:22:08,660 --> 00:22:09,490
Say what?

410
00:22:09,573 --> 00:22:13,077
That stupid can you kicked Spray
Juice all over my brand new manga.

411
00:22:13,160 --> 00:22:15,337
So I want to know what you're
going to do to make this right.

412
00:22:15,420 --> 00:22:16,891
It's a bit grimy a river.

413
00:22:20,000 --> 00:22:23,640
1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7,

414
00:22:23,820 --> 00:22:27,760
8, 9, 10 Alright, let's get started

415
00:22:39,540 --> 00:22:40,370
Breakdown!

416
00:22:40,453 --> 00:22:41,283
Breakdown!

417
00:22:41,366 --> 00:22:44,537
You sure spend a lot of time staring out
into the distance You see anything cool?

418
00:22:44,620 --> 00:22:46,620
I just see plain old Morioh.

419
00:22:48,020 --> 00:22:49,660
Exactly, isn't it grand?

420
00:22:50,020 --> 00:22:53,540
I find this town interesting,
quite interesting indeed.

421
00:22:54,360 --> 00:22:59,200
And so, for most, the summer of
1999 slipped away like any other.

422
00:22:59,440 --> 00:23:03,260
Peace had come to Morioh, making
for some pretty great days.

423
00:23:07,280 --> 00:23:08,820
Hey, did you hear?

424
00:23:09,360 --> 00:23:10,190
Hmm?

425
00:23:10,273 --> 00:23:12,917
Apparently, Rohan got caught
shoplifting from Kameyu.

426
00:23:13,000 --> 00:23:14,380
What a dim shit.

427
00:23:15,140 --> 00:23:17,780
Man, that's freaking crazy. If it's true.

428
00:23:18,020 --> 00:23:19,157
What do you mean by it?

429
00:23:19,240 --> 00:23:20,460
I mean it has to be.

430
00:23:20,620 --> 00:23:22,385
Wait, you don't know for sure?

431
00:23:23,200 --> 00:23:24,030
Dumbass.

432
00:23:24,220 --> 00:23:26,000
Well, come on. Let's bounce.
